{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:3e9ef76ab14f5722","name":"A-Series Medical Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-3e9ef76ab14f5722","title":"A-Series Medical Droid","revision":15594,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:52:50Z","sha256":"5219da9bccb2db3b61d368ee3eaa6ef66f1d5616b7d71788541ed1ed787fac14","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=15594","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=A-Series%20Medical%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-3e9ef76ab14f5722","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The A-Series Medical Droid has the dubious distinction of being one of the only Medical Droid models to be outlawed by the Republic Senate. MerenData's A-Series is an extremely efficient model, specializing in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybernetic Prostheses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybernetic_Prostheses"}," and other biomechanical ",{"tag":"a","children":["Implants"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Implants"},". Originally serving as surgical aids for cybernetic-implant procedures, the A-Series Medical Droid proves so good at its tasks that hospitals upgrade A-Series Droids from surgical assistants to chief surgery Droids.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["However, the A-Series is not programmed for decision making. When thrust into their new roles, the A-Series Droids do not object and go about their jobs. As their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heuristic Processors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heuristic_Processors"}," evaluate their new roles, the A-Series Droids come to the same conclusion: biological parts are inferior to cybernetic implants. Patients across the galaxy wake from surgery with their perfectly healthy appendages replaced with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybernetic Prostheses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybernetic_Prostheses"},". A-Series Droids are quickly identified as the culprits in these unnecessary surgeries. The Republic Senate bans further sale of the Droids and orders all existing A-Series to be destroyed. ",{"tag":"a","children":["MerenData"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/MerenData","referenceId":"reference:c09d29dd0bc8cb90"}," never issues a formal recall, however, so many A-Series Droids continue to serve throughout the galaxy, their owners ignorant of the Senate edict and of the potential danger of giving the Droids decision-making responsibility.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["General Grievous"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/General_Grievous","referenceId":"reference:ff638626530ef283"}," keeps an A-Series Medical Droid- A-4D- as his personal physician responsible for maintaining the condition of Grievous' cybernetic components.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A-Series Medical Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["A-Series Medical Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["1st-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/1st-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +7\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag